apheris-msa 0.9.0
CLI contract: foundry.cli.v1

Tasks:
  fetch-msa - Fetch multiple sequence alignments (MSAs) from a configured provider.
The input format is selected with --input-format.

fasta:
    --input is a FASTA file. One sequence<N>.a3m is written to --output per input
    sequence.

foundry-v1:
    --input is a directory containing one foundry-v1 request JSON plus any provided
    .a3m files. An MSA is ensured for every protein chain, named by its 'msa_path' field
    or a synthesized msa_input_<chain_id>.a3m. Provided MSAs are copied to --output and
    reused; only the still-missing MSAs are generated, and the request (with msa_path
    fields filled in for every protein chain) is written to --output for downstream prediction.

cif:
    --input is a directory of CIF structure files (.cif / .mmcif). One
    <structure>_<chain>.a3m is written to --output per unique protein sequence across all
    structures; chains sharing a sequence (e.g. homodimer chains, or the same structure
    in multiple files) produce a single output file. Non-protein chains are skipped.

openfold3-dataset-v1:
    --input is an OpenFold3 dataset v1 manifest. Train, validation, and test split
    fields are ignored for MSA generation; one <structure-id>_<chain>.a3m is written
    to --output for every protein chain.

For new OpenFold3 workflows, prefer the typed fetch-openfold3-dataset-msa task.
  fetch-openfold3-dataset-msa - Fetch MSAs for an OpenFold3 dataset v1 manifest.

The input is the same JSON/YAML manifest used by OpenFold3 dataset generation. Train,
validation, and test split fields are ignored for MSA generation; one
<structure-id>_<chain>.a3m is written to --output for every protein chain.

This task does not rewrite the manifest. Downstream OpenFold3 data prep receives the
original manifest plus the MSA output directory and matches alignments by sequence.

Use '<task> describe' for details, or add --json for machine output.
